WEBVTT

1
00:00:34.625 --> 00:00:37.041
<b>In the previous verse, Arjuna asked</b>

2
00:00:37.041 --> 00:00:41.458
<b>why humans are driven to </b>
<b>sinful acts even against their will.</b>

3
00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:45.166
<b>Who is the culprit that pushes them toward sin?</b>

4
00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:49.125
<b>In this verse, Krishna reveals this culprit.</b>

5
00:00:54.041 --> 00:00:55.583
<b>Krishna says</b>

6
00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:59.083
<b>the cause is desire or lust,</b>

7
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:02.291
<b>which later transforms into anger.</b>

8
00:01:02.291 --> 00:01:08.541
<b>This desire is deeply sinful and should </b>
<b>be understood as humanity's greatest enemy.</b>

9
00:01:08.541 --> 00:01:11.750
<b>This desire arises from Rajas –</b>

10
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:16.666
<b>the tendency toward worldly </b>
<b>desires and excessive indulgence.</b>

11
00:01:16.666 --> 00:01:24.333
<b>Some might say that fulfilling </b>
<b>these desires would quiet them.</b>

12
00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:25.833
<b>But this isn't true.</b>

13
00:01:25.833 --> 00:01:30.708
<b>Desire is a demon whose </b>
<b>hunger is never satisfied.</b>

14
00:01:30.708 --> 00:01:32.208
<b>It only grows,</b>

15
00:01:32.208 --> 00:01:37.291
<b>and if left unchecked, it eventually </b>
<b>devours all goodness.</b>

16
00:01:37.291 --> 00:01:41.083
<b>It destroys human morality and wisdom.</b>

17
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:43.541
<b>This is why it's called 'Mahasanah' –</b>

18
00:01:43.541 --> 00:01:51.500
<b>the all-devouring one, and</b>
<b>'Mahapapma' - the greatest sin.</b>

19
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.833
<b>Now understand what this desire and lust truly is.</b>

20
00:01:55.833 --> 00:01:58.583
<b>This isn't merely physical desire,</b>

21
00:01:58.583 --> 00:02:04.125
<b>but any selfish desire that craves indulgence -</b>

22
00:02:04.125 --> 00:02:05.291
<b>wealth,</b>

23
00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.083
<b>luxury,</b>

24
00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:06.916
<b>taste,</b>

25
00:02:06.916 --> 00:02:08.250
<b>and much more.</b>

26
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:13.166
<b>It's every selfish desire that only </b>
<b>acknowledges the physical form – </b>

27
00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:17.125
<b>denying the soul, karma, and the divine.</b>

28
00:02:17.125 --> 00:02:26.666
<b>This desire clouds our judgment and</b>
<b>compels us to actions we later regret.</b>

29
00:02:26.666 --> 00:02:31.458
<b>But why does Krishna call it </b>
<b>humanity's greatest enemy?</b>

30
00:02:31.458 --> 00:02:34.916
<b>The greatest enemy isn't one who appears hostile.</b>

31
00:02:34.916 --> 00:02:42.666
<b>The greatest enemy is one who appears as </b>
<b>a friend but stands ready to destroy you.</b>

32
00:02:42.666 --> 00:02:44.791
<b>Desire is exactly like this.</b>

33
00:02:44.791 --> 00:02:46.250
<b>For example –</b>

34
00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:49.958
<b>bodily desire gives pleasure in the moment,</b>

35
00:02:49.958 --> 00:02:53.416
<b>but immediately follows with shame,</b>

36
00:02:53.416 --> 00:02:57.583
<b>and eventually leaves a person hollow inside.</b>

37
00:02:57.583 --> 00:03:03.000
<b>Excessive food and sweets</b>
<b>bring great pleasure at the time,</b>

38
00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.083
<b>but secretly deteriorate your health.</b>

39
00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:13.125
<b>Desire slowly binds you in its grip. </b>
<b>You begin to fall under its control.</b>

40
00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:15.583
<b>And if you don't satisfy its hunger,</b>

41
00:03:15.583 --> 00:03:17.625
<b>this desire will writhe,</b>

42
00:03:17.625 --> 00:03:19.041
<b>compel you,</b>

43
00:03:19.041 --> 00:03:22.000
<b>and finally manifest as anger,</b>

44
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:25.333
<b>destroying your life and relationships.</b>

45
00:03:25.333 --> 00:03:30.666
<b>In truth, desire and lust are the </b>
<b>root of every evil in this world.</b>

46
00:03:30.666 --> 00:03:33.708
<b>The desire for wealth gives birth to greed.</b>

47
00:03:33.708 --> 00:03:38.041
<b>The desire for power and </b>
<b>strength gives birth to ego and pride.</b>

48
00:03:38.041 --> 00:03:43.916
<b>Physical desire gives birth to lust, </b>
<b>even compelling exploitation.</b>

49
00:03:43.916 --> 00:03:47.333
<b>The desire for fame gives birth to jealousy.</b>

50
00:03:47.333 --> 00:03:53.041
<b>This is why Krishna says desire </b>
<b>s humanity's greatest enemy.</b>

51
00:03:53.041 --> 00:03:54.541
<b>The question arises -</b>

52
00:03:54.541 --> 00:03:58.041
<b>will we let this enemy flourish?</b>

53
00:03:58.041 --> 00:03:58.875
<b>Or</b>

54
00:03:58.875 --> 00:04:00.958
<b>will we destroy it?</b>

55
00:04:05.416 --> 00:04:11.958
<b>Think back to a time in your life</b>

56
00:04:11.958 --> 00:04:16.541
<b>when you were consumed by an intense desire.</b>

57
00:04:16.541 --> 00:04:19.875
<b>Those familiar thoughts:</b>

58
00:04:19.875 --> 00:04:24.625
<b>"I won't find peace until I get that new car</b>

59
00:04:24.625 --> 00:04:28.250
<b>secure that promotion at work,</b>

60
00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:32.958
<b>or build a house bigger and </b>
<b>grander than my friend's...</b>

61
00:04:32.958 --> 00:04:35.583
<b>" and the list goes on.</b>

62
00:04:35.583 --> 00:04:37.500
<b>Sounds familiar, doesn't it?</b>

63
00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:44.666
<b>Initially, these desires might seem harmless, </b>
<b>perhaps even inspiring.</b>

64
00:04:44.666 --> 00:04:49.083
<b>After all, they're driving you toward progress.</b>

65
00:04:49.083 --> 00:04:51.625
<b>However,</b>

66
00:04:51.625 --> 00:04:55.833
<b>when these desires remain unfulfilled,</b>

67
00:04:55.833 --> 00:04:59.916
<b>they transform into frustration and anger,</b>

68
00:04:59.916 --> 00:05:04.416
<b>disturbing your inner peace.</b>

69
00:05:04.416 --> 00:05:08.875
<b>And even if these burning desires are fulfilled,</b>

70
00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:10.791
<b>they never cease.</b>

71
00:05:10.791 --> 00:05:15.208
<b>After acquiring one luxury car, </b>
<b>the craving for the next one awakens.</b>

72
00:05:15.208 --> 00:05:18.375
<b>Shortly after gaining a new position,</b>

73
00:05:18.375 --> 00:05:20.958
<b>anxiety about the next promotion</b>
<b>begins to gnaw at you.</b>

74
00:05:20.958 --> 00:05:23.125
<b>It's endless.</b>

75
00:05:23.125 --> 00:05:28.000
<b>Gradually, these cravings, these intense desires,</b>

76
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:32.375
<b>blur the line between right and wrong.</b>

77
00:05:32.375 --> 00:05:37.583
<b>They cloud our judgment.</b>

78
00:05:37.583 --> 00:05:43.416
<b>We begin choosing options </b>
<b>that offer immediate gratification</b>

79
00:05:43.416 --> 00:05:48.833
<b>but lead only to long-term sorrow and regret.</b>

80
00:05:48.833 --> 00:05:51.000
<b>For instance,</b>

81
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.125
<b>the craving for wealth,</b>

82
00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:58.291
<b>this might push someone toward </b>
<b>unethical acts and deception.</b>

83
00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:00.875
<b>Though money might be gained,</b>

84
00:06:00.875 --> 00:06:02.458
<b>but</b>

85
00:06:02.458 --> 00:06:04.625
<b>it leaves a permanent stain on character,</b>

86
00:06:04.625 --> 00:06:07.458
<b>and if caught, brings destruction of reputation,</b>

87
00:06:07.458 --> 00:06:10.750
<b>legal troubles, and shame.</b>

88
00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:12.000
<b>Similarly,</b>

89
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:15.458
<b>when the desire to control</b>
<b>relationships takes over,</b>

90
00:06:15.458 --> 00:06:21.416
<b>it leads to anger, humiliation, and ultimately, </b>
<b>the breakdown of that relationship,</b>

91
00:06:21.416 --> 00:06:26.041
<b>leaving you isolated and alone.</b>

92
00:06:26.041 --> 00:06:28.458
<b>Here's the crucial understanding –</b>

93
00:06:28.458 --> 00:06:30.208
<b>desires aren't wrong,</b>

94
00:06:30.208 --> 00:06:32.958
<b>but obsession with them is.</b>

95
00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:37.583
<b>Nothing - wealth, food, property </b>
<b>- is inherently bad.</b>

96
00:06:37.583 --> 00:06:41.125
<b>It's the hunger for these things </b>
<b>that becomes problematic.</b>

97
00:06:41.125 --> 00:06:42.625
<b>Desires are natural,</b>

98
00:06:42.625 --> 00:06:43.333
<b>but</b>

99
00:06:43.333 --> 00:06:48.416
<b>letting them overpower us is dangerous.</b>

100
00:06:48.416 --> 00:06:53.500
<b>We must question the validity of our desires.</b>

101
00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.375
<b>Is this desire beneficial?</b>

102
00:06:56.375 --> 00:07:02.375
<b>Is it for momentary pleasure</b>
<b>or lasting happiness?</b>

103
00:07:02.375 --> 00:07:05.875
<b>Could it harm others?</b>

104
00:07:05.875 --> 00:07:10.750
<b>Has this desire taken control over me?</b>

105
00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.708
<b>Keep your desires,</b>

106
00:07:12.708 --> 00:07:13.458
<b>but</b>

107
00:07:13.458 --> 00:07:17.208
<b>avoid harmful ones.</b>

108
00:07:17.208 --> 00:07:18.875
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

109
00:07:18.875 --> 00:07:22.166
<b>These questions are essential to ask yourself.</b>

110
00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:30.250
<b>Picture these common scenes:</b>

111
00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:33.791
<b>A child throwing a tantrum</b>

112
00:07:33.791 --> 00:07:38.708
<b>because they can't have what they want</b>

113
00:07:38.708 --> 00:07:45.416
<b>A family member who erupts </b>
<b>in anger over trivial matters</b>

114
00:07:45.416 --> 00:07:54.166
<b>An infant who refuses to eat unless </b>
<b>entertained by colourful programs</b>

115
00:07:54.166 --> 00:07:59.625
<b>These scenes feel familiar, don't they?</b>

116
00:07:59.625 --> 00:08:01.958
<b>Yet</b>

117
00:08:01.958 --> 00:08:11.333
<b>these seemingly ordinary </b>
<b>behaviors signal deeper issues.</b>

118
00:08:11.333 --> 00:08:15.625
<b>They too are small manifestations of desire.</b>

119
00:08:15.625 --> 00:08:22.500
<b>If left unchecked, they can lead to future harm.</b>

120
00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.291
<b>Consider the underlying causes:</b>

121
00:08:25.291 --> 00:08:29.333
<b>Someone in the family might burst into anger</b>

122
00:08:29.333 --> 00:08:37.083
<b>because they're carrying the weight of past hurts,</b>

123
00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:40.875
<b>or perhaps workplace stress has taken its toll.</b>

124
00:08:40.875 --> 00:08:46.833
<b>A child develops the habit of </b>
<b>needing entertainment during meals</b>

125
00:08:46.833 --> 00:08:47.833
<b>because</b>

126
00:08:47.833 --> 00:08:55.000
<b>parents lack quality time to share with them.</b>

127
00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.916
<b>What can be done?</b>

128
00:08:56.916 --> 00:08:59.208
<b>For adults,</b>

129
00:08:59.208 --> 00:09:05.583
<b>understanding and love usually prove effective.</b>

130
00:09:05.583 --> 00:09:10.625
<b>If we can understand why </b>
<b>someone becomes irritated,</b>

131
00:09:10.625 --> 00:09:14.541
<b>and respond with patience instead of reaction,</b>

132
00:09:14.541 --> 00:09:20.958
<b>showing gentleness once they've calmed down,</b>

133
00:09:20.958 --> 00:09:26.500
<b>their anger will gradually diminish over time.</b>

134
00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.666
<b>And what about children?</b>

135
00:09:28.666 --> 00:09:31.500
<b>What can be done there?</b>

136
00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.250
<b>First,</b>

137
00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:37.250
<b>we must examine our own habits.</b>

138
00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:38.791
<b>Usually,</b>

139
00:09:38.791 --> 00:09:45.833
<b>children's behavioural patterns </b>
<b>develop due to parental inattention.</b>

140
00:09:45.833 --> 00:09:54.583
<b>After all, children lack the maturity </b>
<b>to make these decisions independently.</b>

141
00:09:54.583 --> 00:10:01.458
<b>If a habit has become ingrained, </b>
<b>it must be gently unwound.</b>

142
00:10:01.458 --> 00:10:04.541
<b>When a child shows anger,</b>

143
00:10:04.541 --> 00:10:06.708
<b>patience is crucial.</b>

144
00:10:06.708 --> 00:10:09.083
<b>Remember,</b>

145
00:10:09.083 --> 00:10:13.541
<b>if every demand is met,</b>

146
00:10:13.541 --> 00:10:17.500
<b>they'll learn that tantrums </b>
<b>are the path to success.</b>

147
00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:21.208
<b>Some desires should be fulfilled within set rules,</b>

148
00:10:21.208 --> 00:10:23.916
<b>others must be denied.</b>

149
00:10:23.916 --> 00:10:25.166
<b>Remember,</b>

150
00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:28.708
<b>being good parents doesn't mean</b>

151
00:10:28.708 --> 00:10:33.375
<b>fulfilling every inappropriate desire.</b>

152
00:10:33.375 --> 00:10:41.750
<b>Children need to learn they won't </b>
<b>always get everything they crave.</b>

153
00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:47.833
<b>This teaches contentment and </b>
<b>develops patience in them.</b>

154
00:10:47.833 --> 00:10:54.416
<b>And this shouldn't be conveyed as </b>
<b>mere commands, but explained logically.</b>

155
00:10:54.416 --> 00:11:00.291
<b>Have conversations about </b>
<b>why all desires can't be fulfilled.</b>

156
00:11:00.291 --> 00:11:04.166
<b>Meanwhile, choose better alternatives—</b>

157
00:11:04.166 --> 00:11:05.416
<b>sports,</b>

158
00:11:05.416 --> 00:11:07.500
<b>helping with household chores,</b>

159
00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:09.750
<b>reading books...</b>

160
00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:12.000
<b>and above all,</b>

161
00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:16.833
<b>parents spending quality time with their children.</b>

162
00:11:16.833 --> 00:11:20.958
<b>This responsibility supersedes all others.</b>

163
00:11:20.958 --> 00:11:24.666
<b>Your children's lives need your time,</b>

164
00:11:24.666 --> 00:11:29.958
<b>not just your gifts.</b>

165
00:11:29.958 --> 00:11:31.750
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

166
00:11:36.166 --> 00:11:42.541
<b>A successful workplace is one </b>
<b>where everyone feels secure.</b>

167
00:11:42.541 --> 00:11:45.916
<b>This security takes many forms—</b>

168
00:11:45.916 --> 00:11:48.250
<b>protection of people's interests,</b>

169
00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:52.708
<b>assurance against discrimination,</b>

170
00:11:52.708 --> 00:11:58.166
<b>certainty of timely wages...</b>

171
00:11:58.166 --> 00:11:59.708
<b>Consider:</b>

172
00:11:59.708 --> 00:12:04.833
<b>if a workplace fails to provide such security,</b>

173
00:12:04.833 --> 00:12:09.708
<b>will people find fulfillment in working there?</b>

174
00:12:09.708 --> 00:12:17.083
<b>Workplace insecurity stems from </b>
<b>someone's overwhelming desires.</b>

175
00:12:17.083 --> 00:12:21.208
<b>This might be the desire for profit—</b>

176
00:12:21.208 --> 00:12:29.333
<b>where a leader makes excuses to</b>
<b>cut wages for personal gain.</b>

177
00:12:29.333 --> 00:12:33.083
<b>It could be the desire for promotion—</b>

178
00:12:33.083 --> 00:12:39.208
<b>where someone creates obstacles in </b>
<b>another's work to advance themselves.</b>

179
00:12:39.208 --> 00:12:42.791
<b>Even more serious is</b>

180
00:12:42.791 --> 00:12:44.458
<b>this desire,</b>

181
00:12:44.458 --> 00:12:55.125
<b>when someone in leadership develops emotional </b>
<b>or physical attraction toward a colleague.</b>

182
00:12:55.125 --> 00:13:00.250
<b>This attraction might lead to showing favoritism,</b>

183
00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:05.333
<b>burdening others with extra work </b>
<b>to ease that person's load,</b>

184
00:13:05.333 --> 00:13:14.208
<b>or even harassment if the </b>
<b>attraction isn't reciprocated.</b>

185
00:13:14.208 --> 00:13:18.250
<b>Such attraction can manifest </b>
<b>in many harmful ways.</b>

186
00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:23.291
<b>When such personal attractions </b>
<b>surface in the workplace, </b>

187
00:13:23.291 --> 00:13:25.916
<b>their impact isn't limited to </b>
<b>one or two individuals—</b>

188
00:13:25.916 --> 00:13:26.875
<b>but</b>

189
00:13:26.875 --> 00:13:33.041
<b>it affects everyone. The entire atmosphere</b>
<b>becomes uncomfortable.</b>

190
00:13:33.041 --> 00:13:36.625
<b>And if these desires remain unchecked?</b>

191
00:13:36.625 --> 00:13:41.458
<b>The consequences can be devastating.</b>

192
00:13:41.458 --> 00:13:43.333
<b>Therefore, it's essential</b>

193
00:13:43.333 --> 00:13:50.458
<b>that workplace relationships remain respectful </b>
<b>and within professional boundaries.</b>

194
00:13:50.458 --> 00:13:54.500
<b>Control in these relationships cannot be lost.</b>

195
00:13:54.500 --> 00:14:02.791
<b>It's everyone's responsibility, especially </b>
<b>organizational leaders and senior officers,</b>

196
00:14:02.791 --> 00:14:09.916
<b>to maintain a workplace that's safe, fair, </b>
<b>and focused solely on work.</b>

197
00:14:09.916 --> 00:14:15.875
<b>Ignoring these principles can lead to </b>
<b>severe consequences.</b>

198
00:14:15.875 --> 00:14:17.541
<b>Reflect upon this.</b>

